<title>UK: SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITIONS QUARTER-FINAL RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITIONS QUARTER-FINAL RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of African club competitions quarter-final second legs on Sunday:</p>
<p>Confederation of African Football (CAF) Cup</p>
<p>In Kinshasa: </p>
<p>Vita Club (Zaire)  2  Mouloudia Oran (Algeria) 0  (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Lukikama Icham (47th minute) Luende (85th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 80,000</p>
<p>Aggregate score 2-2. Vita won after penalty shoot-out.</p>
<p>In Freetown (played Saturday):</p>
<p>Port Authority (Sierra Leone) 1 Kenya Breweries 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>Aggregate score 1-1. Kenya Breweries won penalty shoot-out 4-2.</p>
<p>African Cup Winners' Cup</p>
<p>In Maiduguri, Nigeria:</p>
<p>Katsina United (Nigeria) 0 Sodigraf (Zaire) 0  (0-0)</p>
<p>Attendance: Not available</p>
<p>Sodigraf won 2-0 on aggregate.</p>
</text>
